course: dictionary
lesson: 2778
title: Feelings: disgust
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Disgust is a strong feeling that something is very unpleasant, dirty or wrong, so you want to turn away. Look at the clues: «At the zoo Kieran bangs on the monkey glass, and a monkey chucks something disgusting at it.» The word disgusting tells you the thing is so unpleasant that you would want to turn away from it.
explain: Disgust can also be a verb. To disgust someone means to make them feel this strong, turned-away feeling. «Faces show basic feelings such as happiness, sadness, fear, anger, surprise and disgust.» Here disgust is a feeling that a face can show. Ask yourself: is the word naming a feeling, or is something making someone feel it?
explain: Stories use disgust to show what a character thinks is horrid or unfair. Watch for phrases like «in disgust», «to my disgust» and «be disgusted by». The clues around them, such as a wrinkled nose or a turned-away head, show you what the character really thinks.
fact: Disgust is one of the basic emotions, and it is often shown by a wrinkled nose.
fact: Disgust protects us from germs and bad food.
fact: «Disgust» is a noun for the feeling; «to disgust» is a verb meaning to make someone feel it.
fact: «Disgusting» describes the thing that causes the feeling, and «disgusted» describes the person who feels it.
fact: Disgust at food is learned from family and culture, and tastes change over time: «lobster was once food for the poor and prisoners in America.»
exercise: «At the zoo Kieran bangs on the monkey glass, and a monkey chucks something disgusting at it.» What does disgusting mean here? | Fast and funny | Shiny and bright | Very quiet and still | *Very unpleasant, the kind of thing you want to turn away from
exercise: Faces show basic feelings such as happiness, sadness, fear, anger, surprise and disgust. Which feeling is often shown by a wrinkled nose? | Surprise | Happiness | Sleepiness | *Disgust
exercise: Why might a character say «in disgust»? | To show they were asleep | To show they were lost | To show they were very happy | *To show they felt a strong, turned-away feeling
test: «Disgust at food is learned from family and culture.» What does this tell you? | Everyone in the world likes the same food | Germs make all food taste nice | *People learn what they find disgusting from the people around them | Food never changes in any country
test: Which word describes the person who feels disgust? | *Disgusted | Disgusting | Disgusts | Disgust
exam: «Lobster was once food for the poor and prisoners in America.» What does this show about disgust? | *Disgust can change over time, as tastes change | Prisoners never ate any food | Lobster has always been loved by everyone | Disgust never changes at all
